{"query":"site:github.com inurl:security/advisories \"XSS\" \"html\"","data":"Security Advisories · mganss/HtmlSanitizer · GitHub (https://github.com/mganss/HtmlSanitizer/security/advisories)\n【turn776137search0】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # Security: mganss/HtmlSanitizer ... ## Security Advisories ...   * XSS in Foreign Content\n\n# Security: mganss/HtmlSanitizer\n\n## Security and quality\n\n  * Overview\n  *   * ### Reporting\n\n    * Security policy\n    * Advisories\n\n## Security Advisories\n\nView information about security vulnerabilities from this repository's maintainers.\n\n[Input: Filter advisories: severity:critical, ecosystem:npm]\n\nClear current search query, filters, and sorts\n\n  * SanitizeDom(string) fails to sanitize attributes merged onto <html>/<head>/<body> wrapper elements\n\nGHSA-x83r-fr5c-qqvj published Nov 2, 2026 by mganss\n\nLow\n\n  * CSS Removal DoS\n\nGHSA-464h-4j8h-q5mf published Aug 7, 2026 by mganss\n\nHigh\n\n  * Bypass via template tag\n\nGHSA-j92c-7v7g-gj3f published Feb 3, 2026 by mganss\n\nModerate\n\n  * XSS in Foreign Content\n\nGHSA-43cp-6p3q-2pc4 published Oct 4, 2023 by mganss\n\nModerate\n\n  * Possible XSS bypass if style tag is allowed\n\nGHSA-8j9v-h2vp-2hhv published Jan 4, 2021 by mganss\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStored XSS in HTML renderers via unescaped violation messages · Advisory · pmd/pmd · GitHub (https://github.com/pmd/pmd/security/advisories/GHSA-8rr6-2qw5-pc7r)\n【turn776137search1】 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: last week; # Stored XSS in HTML renderers via unescaped violation messages ...   * See #6475: [core] Fix stored XSS in VBHTMLRenderer and YAHTMLRenderer\n\n# Stored XSS in HTML renderers via unescaped violation messages\n\nModerate\n\nadangel published GHSA-8rr6-2qw5-pc7r Feb 27, 2026\n\n## Package\n\nnet.sourceforge.pmd:pmd-core (Maven)\n\n## Affected versions\n\n<= 7.21.0\n\n## Patched versions\n\n7.22.0\n\n## Description\n\n### Summary\n\nPMD's `vbhtml` and `yahtml` report formats insert rule violation messages into HTML output without escaping. When PMD analyzes untrusted source code containing crafted string literals, the generated HTML report contains executable JavaScript that runs when opened in a browser.\n\nWhile the default `html` format is not affected via rule violation messages (it correctly uses `StringEscapeUtils.escapeHtml4()`), it has a similar problem when rendering suppressed violations. The user supplied message (the reason for the suppression) was not escaped.\n\n`VBHTMLRenderer.java` line 71 appends `rv.getDescription()` directly into HTML:\n    \n    sb.append(\"<td><font class=body>\").append(rv.getDescription()).append(\"</font></td>\");\n\n`YAHTMLRenderer.java` lines 196–203 does the same via `renderViolationRow()`:\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSecurity Advisories · xdan/jodit · GitHub (https://github.com/xdan/jodit/security/advisories)\n【turn776137search2】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; ## Security Advisories ...   * Cross-site scripting (XSS) via <script> nested in SVG bypasses clean-html sanitization\n\n# Security: xdan/jodit\n\n## Security and quality\n\n  * Overview\n  *   * ### Reporting\n\n    * Security policy\n    * Advisories\n\n## Security Advisories\n\nView known security vulnerabilities and report new vulnerabilities privately to maintainers.\n\n  * Stored XSS: event handlers in a textarea's initial value run before clean-html sanitises it\n\nGHSA-7pxg-rf9q-fg33 published Oct 16, 2026 by xdan\n\nHigh\n\n  * Mutation XSS on value assignment through a <noscript> carrier: sanitized HTML re-parsed with scripting on becomes a live element with an event handler\n\nGHSA-gr86-hxq8-g84q published Oct 8, 2026 by xdan\n\nCritical\n\n  * Stored XSS: event handler attributes survive the background clean-html pass, so HTML entering the editor by drag-and-drop keeps its on* handlers\n\nGHSA-jhhp-r3